# The common case in every RIB ever written: an integer literal in a
# float-declared parameter ("Kd" [1]), and a mixed int/real array in one
# ("Ks" [0.25 1 1 8]), both still coerced through toRtFloatVector unchanged
# now that the parser consults the declared type for the INTEGER case only.
#
# A trailing Sphere follows AGENTS.md's "RIB authoring" section, "The
# desync convention."
Display "malformed_out.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
Surface "plastic" "Kd" [1] "Ks" [0.25 1 1 8]
Sphere 0.5 -0.5 0.5 360
WorldEnd
